 core=[claim('SPHERE-Recover learns from reconstructed images paired with DICOM acquisition metadata. A spatial ViT branch and an FFT-based frequency branch predict sampling dimensions, ratios, and direction. This lets the method estimate sampling-related parameters when headers are unavailable.',6,'Sec. 3.1'),claim('The estimated parameters define a simulated sampling operator. Comparing the original and perturbed image yields a smooth deformation vector field (DVF). SPHERE-Seg uses this field to align features and modulate retention in its Swin-RetNet encoder–decoder.',7,'Secs. 3.2–3.3')],
 io=claim('Reconstructed MRI enters parameter recovery and DVF preprocessing; MRI plus DVF enter SPHERE-Seg; tumor-region masks come out. DICOM metadata supervises recovery training but is not required at deployment.',9,'Sec. 3.3; p. 14 complexity'),
